{"orgCode":"8830","name":"California Law Revision Commission","agencyCode":"8000","agencyName":"General Government","description":"The California Law Revision Commission (Commission) examines California statutory and decisional law for defects and anachronisms and recommends needed reforms. The Commission also undertakes studies as assigned by the Legislature on topics ranging from major policy questions to technical and nonsubstantive statutory reorganizations.\n\nThe Commission consists of seven gubernatorial appointees plus one Senator, one Assembly Member, and the Legislative Counsel. The Commission's work is independent, nonpartisan, and objective.\n\nThe Commission also administers and provides staff support for the Committee on Revision of the Penal Code. The Committee is responsible for studying the Penal Code and recommending reforms to simplify and rationalize California's criminal law and procedures, establish incarceration alternatives, and improve the system of parole and probation. The Committee consists of five gubernatorial appointees, one Senator, and one Assembly Member.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"positions":{"py":8.5,"cy":11.5,"by":11.5},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":2489,"cy":3434,"by":3522}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/8000/8830","kind":"department","name":"California Law Revision Commission","code":"8830","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"positions":{"py":8.5,"cy":11.5,"by":11.5},"byFundType":{},"children":[],"sources":[{"label":"ebudget.ca.gov API: orgProgram/8830","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/api/budget/e/2026-27/orgProgram/8830"},{"label":"Detailed Expenditures by Program (PDF)","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/2026-27/pdf/Enacted/GovernorsBudget/8000/8830.pdf"}],"extra":{"legalCitations":"DEPARTMENT AUTHORITY\n\nGovernment Code, Sections 8280 through 8298."},"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/8000/8830/6740","kind":"program","name":"California Law Revision Commission","code":"6740","amounts":{"py":2489,"cy":3434,"by":3522},"byFun